1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
A quick reference for when the presets don't cover the cadence you need: cron expressions, in four worked examples.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,791
A cron expression is five fields — minute, hour, day of month, month, day of week — each either a number or a star meaning any.

3
00:00:12,791 --> 00:00:16,000
Presets cover the common cases; cron covers everything else.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,313
Weekday mornings at eight: zero, eight, star, star, one through five.

5
00:00:20,313 --> 00:00:25,000
The weekday field takes a range, so Monday through Friday is one dash five.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Every four hours: zero minutes past, and a slash-four on the hour field means every fourth hour starting from zero — midnight, four, eight, and on.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Monthly, on the first at nine: zero, nine, one in the day-of-month field, star for month, star for weekday.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Friday evening at five: zero, seventeen for the 24-hour clock, star, star, and five for Friday in the weekday field.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,956
Schedules covered.

10
00:00:52,956 --> 00:00:58,000
Now the browser — a real, model-visible window your agent can drive from inside a conversation.

